<http://data.silknow.org/object/8358c15f-3f55-3bcf-9729-985f641b2bf2>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "Notes & Queries: 8th series, Vol: II, p.378\n<i>Domestic Needlework</i>, 1926. pl. XVI, p. 54, describes the pincushion as 'Scotch 1700-30'.\nA note in the departmental register states that this pincushion is nearly identical with two lent to the Stuart exhibition at the New Gallery, London, in 1889 by the Duchess of Albany, and Col. R. Wyatt, catalogue numbers 539 and 1073 respectively. See colour plate in 'The Royal House of Stuart', by William Gibb, plate XXXIV, I.  The pincushion once belonging to the Duchess of Albany is now in the collection of the Ashmolean Museum, Oxford."@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/ad91da4a-2c49-3a67-a4fc-7aea0f41a5f5> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Notes & Queries: 8th series, Vol: II, p.378\n<i>Domestic Needlework</i>, 1926. pl. XVI, p. 54, describes the pincushion as 'Scotch 1700-30'.\nA note in the departmental register states that this pincushion is nearly identical with two lent to the Stuart exhibition at the New Gallery, London, in 1889 by the Duchess of Albany, and Col. R. Wyatt, catalogue numbers 539 and 1073 respectively. See colour plate in 'The Royal House of Stuart', by William Gibb, plate XXXIV, I.  The pincushion once belonging to the Duchess of Albany is now in the collection of the Ashmolean Museum, Oxford."@en .

